  "description": "Some subtle clues the market is giving...that are historically not good...",
  "body_html": "<p>I am not saying the top is in. </p><p>I am not saying to sprint to your computer and sell now. </p><p>Nor do I make any claims that I can time the market perfectly. </p><p>The p<em><strong>oint of this piece is to warn you, ahead of time</strong></em>, and prepare you. This is a discussion piece! We have had a ton of euphoria for several months now…but I see some troubling signs in the market right now. These warning signals were what got me (and all of our trading tribe) out of the Markets back on <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stock-market-update-19-december-24\">December 20<sup>th</sup>, 2024</a> and <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/be-cautious-dont-take-losses?r=4z8lgl\">February 19<sup>th</sup>, 2025</a>…before the large scale pull backs in the market. </p><p>Trust me, I don’t enjoy this…but its important to candidly review this, with no emotion. Understandably, its the party coming to an end. No one likes that. The good news though…is if we do start to break down, one particular stock looks really primed for a short… I wrote <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/2-popular-stocksto-short?r=4z8lgl\">about Costco and Walmart previously, here</a>. Check that out…it is within range for shorting…and I bring it up because it drives this analysis as well. </p><p>So…why am I sending out the warning signal now…</p>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
  "truncated_body_text": "I am not saying the top is in.",
